{{!
    @template mod_datalynx/field_itinerary_app

    Display of a datalynxfield_itinerary field in the Moodle App.

    The app runs none of the plugin's JavaScript, so no map is drawn: the stops are listed and
    a link opens the journey in the maps app of the device. The link carries the coordinates
    the viewer may see (rounded when the field coarsens them); nothing else in this output
    holds coordinates.

    Context variables required for this template:
    * waypoints - Ordered stops, each with address, isfirst, islast.
    * approximate - Whether the coordinates in the link are rounded.
    * lengthlabel - Human readable straight-line journey length.
    * hasroute - Whether a routed distance and travel time are known.
    * routelabel - Human readable road distance.
    * traveltimelabel - Human readable travel time.
    * mapurl - Link that opens the journey in a maps service.

    Example context (json):
    {
        "waypoints": [
            {"address": "Wien Hauptbahnhof", "isfirst": true, "islast": false},
            {"address": "HLFS", "isfirst": false, "islast": true}
        ],
        "approximate": true,
        "lengthlabel": "Approximately 145.2 km",
        "hasroute": true,
        "routelabel": "195.3 km by road",
        "traveltimelabel": "Travel time approx. 2 h 10 min",
        "mapurl": "https://www.openstreetmap.org/directions?engine=fossgis_osrm_car&route=48.19%2C16.38%3B47.07%2C15.42"
    }
}}
<div class="datalynx-itinerary datalynx-itinerary--app">
    <ol class="datalynx-itinerary__stops">
        {{#waypoints}}
            <li class="datalynx-itinerary__stop{{#isfirst}} datalynx-itinerary__stop--start{{/isfirst}}{{#islast}} datalynx-itinerary__stop--end{{/islast}}">
                <span class="datalynx-itinerary__address">{{address}}</span>
            </li>
        {{/waypoints}}
    </ol>
    <p class="datalynx-itinerary__meta">
        {{^hasroute}}{{lengthlabel}}{{/hasroute}}
        {{#hasroute}}{{routelabel}} · {{traveltimelabel}}{{/hasroute}}
        {{#approximate}} · {{#str}}precision_approximate, datalynxfield_itinerary{{/str}}{{/approximate}}
    </p>
    {{#mapurl}}
        <p class="datalynx-itinerary__maplink">
            <a href="{{mapurl}}" class="btn btn-outline-primary btn-sm" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer noopener">
                {{#str}}openinmaps, datalynxfield_itinerary{{/str}}
            </a>
        </p>
    {{/mapurl}}
</div>
